  "result": "I found the cause of the `#` bug and have a plan for the fix, but I haven't changed any code. Plan mode blocks edits, and my attempt to load the plan-approval tool found nothing, so I can't submit the plan for approval.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:603` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment character by default. Everything after an unquoted `#` is silently dropped. For example, `cli a#b` becomes `['cli', 'a']`. In Fish, an incomplete word like `#foo` splits to an empty list and raises `IndexError`.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. Add `lex.commenters = \"\"` after `lex.whitespace_split = True` in `split_arg_string`.\n2. Add test cases to `tests/test_parser.py::test_split_arg_string`:\n   - `cli a#b`\n   - `cli #foo`\n   - `cli a #b c`\n   - `cli \"a#b\"`\n3. Add a CHANGES entry.\n4. Verify with `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-soft-crab.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll make the changes.",
